WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.266
Hello! In today's Cloud Minute I'll be demonstrating 
how to get help with gcloud

00:00:03.266 --> 00:00:05.366
gcloud is the command line too that you use to access

00:00:05.366 --> 00:00:07.500
and configure your Google Cloud Platform resources

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.566
If you are ever unsure how to use a gcloud command

00:00:09.566 --> 00:00:11.833
just type the command followed by --help

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.966
This gives you some basic information about how 
to use the command

00:00:14.966 --> 00:00:19.166
For example this page says to use gcloud 
followed by a group and then a command

00:00:19.166 --> 00:00:19.200
a group and then a command.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.366
And if I scroll down a little bit 

00:00:20.366 --> 00:00:23.066
I can see the different groups I can use with the gcloud command

00:00:23.366 --> 00:00:25.433
One group pretty much everyone uses is config

00:00:25.433 --> 00:00:27.266
Here's what the help looks like for config

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:30.266
And here you can see that the possible commands for config are

00:00:30.266 --> 00:00:31.100
list

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:31.900
set

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:32.966
and unset

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.100
If I want to know how to use the list command I can type

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.900
gcloud config list --help

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.133
The help page says that there's a --all option

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:44.200
that will show me all the different properties 
that I can set with gcloud config

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.266
So let's look at that

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.933
And now you can see all the different properties
that you can set with gcloud config

00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:53.200
So if you are ever confused or stuck when using gcloud

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.166
try out the built in help

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:55.633
Thanks for watching

00:00:55.633 --> 00:00:58.000
please check out some of our other Cloud Minute videos

